WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.350
Picture two water companies,
each digging up your street

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.160
to lay its own pipes.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.000
It sounds like competition.

4
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.550
It also sounds like paying
for the same network twice.

5
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:15.100
Now picture a company with
40,000 employees in 30 countries,

6
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.300
where decisions take months.

7
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.820
Why can a giant firm
make things more cheaply

8
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.610
than a small one, and when
does size start to hurt?

9
00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.640
In this mission, you'll trace
the long-run average total

10
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.950
cost curve as a firm grows.

11
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.480
Then you'll see why some
markets can be supplied

12
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.150
most cheaply by just one network.

13
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:37.640
Your mission: explain
when bigger means cheaper,

14
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.160
and when it backfires.
